55,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Textiles (A) sounds lovely and local, but Maritime (C) might have high transport costs for those loans.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"City Under Excavation (D) has a working bench, which Shion's data suggests visitors love, but it might stress the lab.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Light and Motion (B) fits the ""mechanism"" trend, but Shizue warned us about powered display failures.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Light and Motion (B) uses overhead rigging; I'm worried about the suspended bay's weight limit and evening hire damage.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Maritime (C) involves many loans from partner collections, which means more paperwork risks and shipping delays.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Victoria, would the ""working bench"" in Candidate D actually help the lab, or just add more work?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"It might be a way to make the backlog visible, but the lab is still understaffed. However, Textiles (A) is very safe.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Shion,,Textiles (A) is too static. The visitor slips say people want someone present. Candidate D's working bench is perfect.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"Candidate D is local finds, so transport is minimal and weight is manageable. It's much safer than B or C.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"I like Candidate A for its simplicity, but D's local nature avoids the shipping disasters I'm worried about.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Mio,,I like the idea of the working bench in D! It's exciting and probably cheaper than shipping huge maritime models.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"If the volunteers are town historians, they would be perfect for the City Under Excavation (D) or Textiles (A).","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Shion,,"D is the clear winner for engagement. It has the ""human"" element and the ""discovery"" aspect.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I support D. It respects the structural limits and doesn't interfere with evening hires as much as rigging would.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Local finds mean less paperwork and fewer shipping headaches. D is a sensible choice.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for D!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree, D is the most balanced.","{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Shion,,D it is.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Asuka,,My vote is for D.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will also vote for D.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
